# hwrev.ini -- manual board override for RK3326
#
# Rename to hwrev.ini in the root of this (FAT) partition to use it.
#
# U-Boot identifies the device from SARADC channel 0 and sets the variables
# below.  Several RK3326 handhelds read within a few counts of each other, so
# detection can pick the wrong one -- and a device with no range at all falls
# through to a generic entry.  Every line here is a U-Boot command, run right
# after detection, so anything set here wins.
#
# THE SHORT FORM: name the board and nothing else.
#
#   setenv hwrev mymini
#
# U-Boot then applies that board's whole profile and throws the SARADC result
# away.  Prefer this over listing the variables by hand: a file that corrects
# hwrev but forgets, say, dtb_kernel leaves the device running half one board's
# settings and half another's, which is worse than the misdetection it was
# meant to fix.  Boards with a profile:
#
#   v10  v11  v10-go3  r36s  rppocket  xf40h  gkd-pixel2  batlexp-g350
#   rg351v  mymini  magicx-mini-m  r36max
#
# Lines after the board name still override individual variables, so the long
# form below remains available for a board with no profile yet.
#
#   hwrev          board name; reaches Linux as board=<hwrev> and becomes
#                  /boot/boot/knulli.board's counterpart for capabilities
#   dtb_uboot      DTB U-Boot uses for its own display init; path included,
#                  normally dtbs/<name>.dtb on this partition
#   dtb_kernel     DTB handed to Linux; path included, boot/<name>.dtb
#   logo_filename  boot splash matching the panel resolution.  Artwork is named
#                  WITHOUT a directory -- it always comes from logos/, because
#                  logo_suffix below builds filenames by pattern and so cannot
#                  carry one.
#   logo_suffix    suffix for the status images (logos/low_battery_<suffix>.bmp
#                  and the battery_N charge animation)
#   fb_rotate      console/SDL rotation: 0, 1, 2 or 3
#   preload_boot   set to 1 on boards whose MMC stops working after U-Boot
#                  applies the kernel DTB ("MMC: no card present" followed by
#                  a stall right after the splash).  Kernel, initrd and DTB are
#                  then staged from boot.ini before that happens.  Defaults on
#                  for R36S, off elsewhere.
#   lcd_vcc_gpio   GPIO index (bank * 32 + pin) of a GPIO-gated LCD supply that
#                  U-Boot fails to drive itself -- the symptom is "gpio A13 not
#                  reserved" / "Can't set regulator ... gpio to: 1" just before
#                  the DSI init commands.
#
# To find your device's ADC value, watch the serial console for:
#   adc0 (hw rev) <value>
#
# Worked example -- R36 Max.  This one is not optional: the R36 Max carries the
# XF40H design with a smaller battery, and on both boards SARADC channel 0 is
# the left stick's X axis rather than a board-ID divider, so detection reads the
# stick and lands on xf40h.  Without this line the fuel gauge is told the pack
# is 3228 mAh when it is 2832, so the battery percentage reads high.  Charging
# itself is unaffected -- both boards stop at 4.2 V / 800 mA.
#
#setenv hwrev r36max

# Worked example -- XiFan MyMini, which reads ADC 513 and so is detected as an
# RG351V.  Uncomment to use:
#
#setenv hwrev mymini

# Worked example -- MagicX Mini-M.  Its profile covers the panel; preload_boot
# is separate because it depends on the DTB it adopts (an RG351V-derived one
# that breaks MMC after dm_scan_fdt):
#
#setenv hwrev magicx-mini-m
#setenv preload_boot 1
#setenv lcd_vcc_gpio 13

# Long form, for a board with no profile of its own.  Every variable must be
# given -- whatever is left out keeps the misdetected board's value:
#
#setenv hwrev myboard
#setenv dtb_uboot dtbs/rk3326-myboard.dtb
#setenv dtb_kernel boot/rk3326-myboard-linux.dtb
#setenv logo_filename logo_640x480.bmp
#setenv logo_suffix _640x480
#setenv fb_rotate 0
